WEBVTT

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:20.330
What?

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:23.710
Together again, huh?

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:25.830
I'm happy about it, at least.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.630
Y-Yeah, me too.

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.670
Getting stuck with you was the last thing I wanted, Takayama.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:32.590
But...

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:38.260
The top brass can't be that terrible if they were smart enough to put me in the PSF.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:39.760
PSF?

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:43.770
Looks like I'm the only one that needs introducing, then.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.520
I'll be in charge of you all from now on.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:54.240
I'm Tokyo Central Railroad Public Security Force, Fourth Peacekeeper Squad Leader, Nana Iida.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:59.160
Oh, and everyone calls us K4, as in Fourth "Keeper" Squad.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.450
And please don't call me "Squad Leader".

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:04.330
Ms. Iida is fine.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:08.250
The PSF Fourth Keeper Squad?

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:44.030
We received notice not too long ago that
an explosive was planted in Yokohama Station.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:47.330
While this may be a direct challenge to us,

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:50.580
the most important thing is to stop
this affront to our customers' safety.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.420
This criminal action must be punished severely.

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:57.840
It is our job to protect JNR customers.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.840
All set to go.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:04.720
Tokaido south-bound special line, all green!

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:05.720
Start the train!

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:06.930
Starting the train.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.200
<i>This can't be happening.</i>

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:35.000
<i>F-Farewell, O peaceful life of a JNR employee.</i>

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.250
<i>I was supposed to be a train driver.</i>

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.460
We should deploy too, Ms. Iida!

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.470
We have a different job.

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:49.600
Thank goodness!

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:51.810
What do you mean, "thank goodness"?

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:54.640
Well, we're basically just holding the fort.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.520
How're we part of the PSF
if we're not right in the action?

00:04:58.520 --> 00:04:59.820
Excuse me!

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:03.610
Where might I find the bullet train platform?

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.450
It's right that way.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:07.320
P-Please excuse her!

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.080
Allow me to take you there.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:10.580
Shall we?

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:12.200
Thank you.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:23.590
She's in your hands, then.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:24.510
Very well.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:25.760
Thanks a lot.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:28.260
You be careful now, ma'am.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:40.150
What's the matter?

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:42.190
Aw, man.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:43.780
Everything all right?

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:47.910
I can't get him to stop crying.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:49.820
A lost kid, huh?

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:52.790
What do we do?

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:00.420
You got separated from your mommy, didn't you?

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:10.430
There, there.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:14.180
Really helps to have a girl
around at times like these.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:22.900
What is this? It's like we're mall cops!

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.820
Mall cops? That's a clever way to put it!

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:27.360
Enough with the jokes, please.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:29.860
I wanted to work for the Public Security Force!

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:33.030
Keeping Tokyo Station safe is a vital part of public security!

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:35.160
But what I <i>want</i> isвЂ”

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.710
You know, Ms. Sakurai...

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:41.130
I think you're a little mistaken here.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:44.300
Our job is not to fight!

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:52.050
So I'll be taking this from you.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:57.140
Logging one found bag, huh?

00:06:57.140 --> 00:07:00.060
With clothes and toiletries inside.

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:05.400
No one's come to pick this one up?

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:09.070
Actually, I just got a call from the owner.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:10.610
That's great!

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:13.950
They said to keep it here.
They'll pick it up today.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:15.660
Good for you, huh?

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:22.670
What's up?

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:26.000
Nothing.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.760
You guys are working hard, I see.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:31.590
About time for lunch, don't you think?

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:33.180
We'll take shifts, thenвЂ”

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:33.930
Whoa!

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:35.300
Let's go, Haruka.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.970
You get to go first? How's that fair?

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:40.640
Pipe down. Ever hear of "ladies first"?

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.190
What?

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:55.450
Did you enjoy your lunch?

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:58.450
Thank you so much for treating us.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:01.460
Not a problem.
I invited you out, after all.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:01.790
Here's your order.
Not a problem.
I invited you out, after all.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:03.250
And here's the special!
Here's your order.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:04.170
And here's the special!

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.000
That looks great!

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:09.000
Excuse me.

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:15.340
It's a special dessert that uses liquid nitrogen.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:17.050
This place is famous for it.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:20.020
Please enjoy while it's still cold.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:32.900
And?

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:35.610
It's so cold and crunchy!

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:36.530
Yum.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:40.160
Sweets are the best when you've got something on your mind.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.590
They're taking too long.

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:49.550
How far could they have gone for lunch?

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:51.340
It's all right, isn't it?

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:53.800
Let's finish this up before they get back.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:55.510
Takayama!

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:11.400
We just received a call from the perpetrator.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:14.860
They claim to have planted
an explosive inside Tokyo Station.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:17.410
So that was just a demonstration, huh?

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:18.700
Classic strategy.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:21.700
But they said Yokohama firstвЂ”

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.500
Obviously this was their real target.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:24.370
No way.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:27.670
Stationmaster Katamachi,
what were their demands?

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:32.880
They want 100 million yen in exchange for telling us where the bomb is.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.840
100 million yen? That's crazy!

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:38.930
Well, see, um...

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:43.060
Tokyo Station makes about 300 million yen a day.

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:46.020
So it's, uh, not really all that crazy.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.060
What?

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:53.320
If we don't hand over the money by 3 p.m.,
they'll set off a giant explosion.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:54.150
What?

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:57.570
That's less than an hour from now!

00:09:57.570 --> 00:10:03.330
I contacted Captain Gonou, but even returning from Yokohama immediately as she is,

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.290
the Disposal Squad might not make it in time.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.620
We have to hurry and
evacuate the customers!

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:09.080
We can't!

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:12.000
We run the risk of inciting a panic.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:12.920
ButвЂ”

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:17.630
This is <i>Tokyo</i> Station, the very heart of the city. All traffic will come to a halt!

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:24.350
Perhaps you should prepare the money, Stationmaster Katamachi.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:25.810
Very well.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:32.650
We're giving in to their demands?

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:39.280
As a JNR employee, your first priority is always the customer's safety.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:44.870
If only we could figure out where the
bomb is before Captain Gonou gets back.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.790
Maybe we should search for it ourselves.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.380
Then search we shall.

00:10:58.010 --> 00:11:02.140
But <i>only</i> search.

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:06.430
I'll gather the other employees and tell them to look for any suspicious objects.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:13.400
If we can't defuse the situation by 2:50 p.m., we'll pay the bomber.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:14.440
Right.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:27.410
Whoa, seriously?

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:32.630
The station has more than 3,000 coin lockers just on the inside.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:34.960
It won't be easy, but let's give it our all!

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:41.720
Koumi, check this one.

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:42.590
Okay!

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:45.890
What's gotten up your butt?

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:48.140
The spirit of the PSF awaken in you?

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:49.180
No.

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:54.400
I just want our customersвЂ”everyoneвЂ”
to be able to ride the rails safely.

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:08.160
Track 2, rapid transit to Toyota, will be departing soon.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.830
It will be stopping at every stop until Toyota.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.080
Please get on and wait for departure.

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.930
Nope. Not here, either.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:26.850
Haruka, how many does that make?

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:28.560
We've checked 368 lockers.

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:30.470
What do we do?

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:32.560
We'll never make it at this rate.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:35.270
Are we sure it's the lockers?

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:36.060
Huh?

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:37.730
Just think about it.

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:40.070
Would they really repeat themselves?

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:42.570
Then where's the real thing?

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:45.570
In the last place we'd think to look, I bet.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:47.280
Whoa!

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.490
Sorry.

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:49.490
Um...

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:51.950
Yes, this is Koumi.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:54.710
Um, what do youвЂ”

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:55.170
Huh?

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:56.000
WhatвЂ”

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:56.710
Hello?

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.130
Hello?!

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:01.210
Did they find it?

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:02.260
No.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:06.930
The dog at the Lost & Found Center
suddenly started barking and won't stop.

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:10.220
That's it!

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:12.020
That's gotta be the bomb!

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:13.230
How are you so sure?

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:15.480
Instinct.

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:18.400
We'll just have to trust you.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:19.480
What?!

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:27.320
That's a pretty big bag for such a small dog.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:29.200
How long has it been barking?

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:31.490
For about 30 minutes.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:34.870
I was on the phone with its owner when it suddenly started barking.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.710
Now that's suspicious.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.100
Hey, Sakurai!

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.060
What is it?

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:53.680
This is the bomb.

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:54.220
What?

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:55.680
I knew it!

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:58.060
Close this place right now.

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:00.190
Haruka, tell Squad Leader Iida
we have an emergency!

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:02.570
Iwaizumi, evacuate any nearby customers!

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:02.940
Right!

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:03.940
On it!

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:06.490
We've gotta take care of the bombвЂ”

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:07.700
Idiot!

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:08.820
Stop moving!

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.120
Don't you know bombs always come with traps?

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:12.790
One wrong move, and "kaboom"!

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:14.410
N-No way.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.710
Don't worry.

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:18.000
I have a plan.

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:22.420
You can let go now.

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:23.670
R-Right.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:36.930
Is this smart? If it blows upвЂ”

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:39.390
If that happens, we're both screwed.

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:41.360
H-Hey, Sakurai! Stop!

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:50.660
There it is.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:52.870
Good. Now we can wait
for the Disposal Squad.

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:53.530
Can't.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:55.370
Why?!

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:58.370
We've only got 15 minutes till this thing blows.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:14:59.370
Fifteen?

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:03.130
That's exactly when we're supposed to hand over the money!

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:07.550
They must have been planning to use
the explosion as cover for their escape.

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.970
H-Hey, don't be crazy!

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:14.170
It's do or die here.

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:26.730
You can run away if you're scared.

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:29.150
What other choice do I have but to help you?

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:33.530
If this blows up here, it'll hurt the customers!

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:36.990
Your life, your choice.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:41.830
Can you really defuse it, Sakurai?

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:44.960
My dad taught me how, at least.

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:47.920
But I've never done it in real life before.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:56.890
What are you two doing?

00:15:57.470 --> 00:15:58.640
Koumi.

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:03.270
Ms. Iida said not to touch the bomb!

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:05.520
Sorry, too late for that.

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:13.530
Keep going! Walk toward the exit!

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:19.580
Next, I have to cut the yellow and white wires simultaneously.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.040
Simultaneously?

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:24.830
I'll push the white wire in, so you make the yellow wire line up with it.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:26.920
The yellow wire...

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:32.550
Get closer. You should reach if your arm is on my chest.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:34.840
ButвЂ”

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:37.510
Hurry up!

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:40.430
What're you doing?!

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:42.640
All right, already!

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:45.940
Takayama...

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:47.110
Aoi...

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:08.420
What's wrong, Sakurai?

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:09.960
Which one do I cut?

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:11.880
Don't ask me!

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:15.720
Only the person who made this would know which one to cut.

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:16.680
You pick.

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:18.640
I don't know...

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:25.640
O-Oh! Cut the pink one, like the "cherry blossoms" in your name.

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:26.600
I'm cutting the red one.

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:27.400
Why?!

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:29.860
Crap!

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:31.940
I told you, didn't I?

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:33.440
Get off my case!

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:35.030
Just cut the pink one already.

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:39.950
It's too late. If I cut it now, it'll blow up.

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:42.290
What do we do, then?

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:45.160
Sakurai!

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:47.460
Hold this down.

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:49.130
Now!

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:50.210
R-Right.

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:54.420
Wh-Where are you going?

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:56.720
Don't you let go of that.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:58.470
S-Sakurai!

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:00.930
Trust me.

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:04.100
H-Hey!

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:15.940
Takayama, is there anything I can do?

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:22.330
Could you make sure that no one's around to get hurt by this thing?

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:26.830
Not that! Isn't there anything I can do for <i>you</i>?

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.120
Koumi.

00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:36.840
Our customers come first.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.970
That's what we were taught, right?

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:21.510
Sorry I took so long!

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:24.010
Sakurai!

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:28.270
It's so cold!

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:30.270
Suck it up! And don't let go!

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:44.280
Sakurai!

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:46.410
Don't worry. Trust me!

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:51.920
Stop!

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:09.390
The timer stopped.

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:29.620
Arrest him!

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:31.250
Don't touch me!

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:32.040
Damn you!

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:35.790
Get off!

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:42.260
I have a few questions for you. Come with us.

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:49.760
It's over.

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:54.440
What did you go and get, Sakurai?

00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:56.940
Liquid nitrogen.

00:20:56.940 --> 00:21:00.190
I cooled the circuit board
so electricity couldn't flow.

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:07.990
H-Hey!

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:12.410
Takayama, you can forget about this later.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:14.920
Sorry.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:17.710
Just let me for a little.

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:24.420
Thanks for trusting me.

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:32.600
M-Me, deputy squad leader?

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:36.600
Yup. You really proved yourself today.

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:38.060
Work hard!

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:41.820
Seriously? <i>This</i> spineless wimp?

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:43.860
It's fine by me.

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:45.320
You, Koumi?

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:48.320
Y-Yeah. I think it's a good idea.

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:50.780
Then that's that.

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:52.740
Okay?

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:57.290
Fine.

00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:08.340
I think I'm getting even further from becoming a train driver.

00:23:40.600 --> 00:23:43.520
The JNR Tsurumi Line, nationalized during the war,

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:47.280
was originally a private railway
known as Tsurumi Harbor Railways,

00:23:47.280 --> 00:23:51.280
responsible for freight transport in the Keihin Industrial Zone.

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:53.870
It's one of the railways that symbolizes our postwar economic boom.

00:23:53.870 --> 00:23:57.490
There is even a stop along the line with a Showa-themed amusement parkвЂ”

00:23:57.490 --> 00:23:59.160
Okay, that's enough.

00:23:59.160 --> 00:24:02.000
The next episode is about me and my train-sound-remixing friends.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:05.670
Rail Wars, Episode Three: Pretty Cool.

00:24:05.670 --> 00:24:09.260
The Hokutosei running through the snowy landscape is a thing of beauty, don't you agree?
